# Dedicated CLI compile server variant (opt-in speed path, separate from
# vshaxe). Start once:
#   haxe --wait 7822
# Caches macro-expanded modules between runs so only changed modules
# recompile. If a stale synthesized-type error appears, restart the
# server.
#
# Only run this file if you know a COMPATIBLE server is listening on
# 7822 (started from this checkout). A stray or mismatched server on
# that port answers --connect without error and silently skips the
# build (exit 0, no bin/test.n written, no output) - use plain
# test.hxml as the safe default; it never depends on one.
#
# The lint compiler oracle now has its OWN warm server (apqlint.json
# `compilerOracleServer`, anyparse.check.CompilerServer). That is not
# this file: it owns the server it talks to, proves the port answers
# as a compilation server before believing any verdict, and re-runs a
# rejection cold - the three things a hand-started --connect here does
# not do. The warning above still stands for THIS file.
--connect 7822
test-common.hxml
-neko bin/test.n
--cmd neko bin/test.n
